It occurs to me that were I my character, facing the dungeons with
naught but my wits to protect me, given the insane number of items to
identify and keep track of, I'd want to keep tabs on things as best I
can. Knowing that in the course of my dungeon delvings I'm likely to
find items and creatures that can suck the thoughts out of my head, I'd
want to keep some notes handy. Hence I'm proposing the Book of Notes.

A book of notes is created when the character applies a magic marker to
a blank spellbook and specifies "notes" as the book they'd like to
write. There is no chance of failure for writing a book of notes,
unless the character is confused or hallucinating, in which case the
result is always a cursed book of notes. Writing a book of notes
requires 1 magic marker charge per 2 mapped levels + 1 charge per "N"
items identified (as an arbitrary number, let's say 5), meaning that a
book of notes grows increasingly costly to write as the game
progresses. However, in the case of a Mind Flayer attack or accidental
reading of a scroll of amnesia, it allows a player to recover their
lost information up to the point the book was created.

Reading an uncursed book of notes takes 1 turn per charge used to write
the book. A blessed book of notes takes only one turn to read and
excercises Wisdom. Reading a cursed book of notes abuses wisdom, causes
confusion for 1-(number of charges used) rounds and has a small chance
of causing amnesia as per a cursed scroll of amnesia.

Books of Notes have a specific appearance ("You see here a wire-bound
spellbook"). They are never randomly generated, however they may appear
in bones files. When found in a bones file, they will always be cursed
and cannot be uncursed ("It's as though they were writing about a
totally different dungeon!"). Wishing for a Book of Notes always
results in the creation of a cursed book of notes as per a bones file
find.

After a book of notes is written, it is complete and cannot be added
to. #dipping a book of notes in uncursed water or zapping a wand of
cancellation at it creates a blank spellbook.

It is possible to write scrolls of notes. However, reading a scroll of
notes, whether blessed, uncursed, or cursed, simply generates a random
reminder message. "Remember to take the trash out." "Remember to feed
<pet>." "Remember not to weild a cockatrice corpse without gloves."


